// No candidate proof, identity or official marking scheme is shipped in this report.
const trials = [
  {model:'Hosted Llama 3.3 70B · original reviewer',n:6,offered:0,exact:null,near:null,mae:null},
  {model:'On-device Qwen3 1.7B',n:24,offered:12,exact:3,near:5,mae:'2.83 / 7'}
];
const counted=(num,n)=>num==null?'—':num+' / '+n;
export function benchmarkReport(){return `<section class="card spacer" aria-labelledby="benchmark-heading"><span class="eyebrow">MARKING STUDY · NOVEMBER 2026</span><h2 id="benchmark-heading">How close are the marks?</h2><p>Each proof was read twice without access to the human score. A model offered one mark only when both readings agreed on every criterion. Exact matches, marks within one point, and average absolute error are measured only on the proofs that received a mark.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Grader</th><th scope="col">Offered a mark</th><th scope="col">Exact</th><th scope="col">Within 1</th><th scope="col">Avg. error</th></tr></thead><tbody>${trials.map(t=>`<tr><th scope="row">${t.model}</th><td>${counted(t.offered,t.n)}</td><td>${counted(t.exact,t.offered)}</td><td>${counted(t.near,t.offered)}</td><td>${t.mae??'—'}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>The original hosted reviewer returned no agreed marks on the six hard proofs. Ten of twelve readings returned a response; only two passed validation. The two individual marks were both 7/7, against human marks of 5 and 0. There is no exact-match rate when no marks were offered.</p><p>The local model abstained on 12 proofs, including one interrupted run. Of its six full-mark proposals, none matched the human score. One gave 7/7 against 0/7. Treat it as experimental feedback.</p><p class="tiny">The <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2610.36767v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TROJAN-Bench(H) study</a> provides researcher-written variants of six 2025 USAMO proofs and expert research marks from 0–7. These are not official grades on contestant scripts. The original hosted six are a subset of the device sample. No result here establishes accuracy on CMI, ISI or RMO exam papers.</p></section>`;}
